WEBVTT

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.630
Some libraries only work when a
provider wraps your whole app.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:15.000
A custom app wrapper puts your own
component at the very top of your React Native app.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.200
In Studio, add a

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.940
file named customapp.rapper.js
to the web app folder.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.220
Export a default component that takes
children and wraps them in your provider.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.420
Here, that's Tan Stack Query.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.820
Create the client outside the
component, so it survives an app reload.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.640
On the next build, WaveMaker copies your
wrapper into the generated app and wraps

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.000
everything with it.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.010
Use it for any library
that needs a provider.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:59.450
Data caching, state, gestures, error
reporting, analytics, or payment SDKs.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.210
Nest as many providers as you like.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.150
Just make sure the innermost
one renders children.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:12.730
And remember, the wrapper sits outside
WaveMaker, so variables, themes, and

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.850
localization aren't available inside it.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.970
One file and your whole app is wrapped.
